  <Placemark>
    <name>Rochers-de-Naye (above Montreux) [70 CHF return]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Rochers de Naye 2042 m - top station</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The biggest single descent reachable from Lausanne in under 90 minutes: 1500 m of vertical from 2042 m down to the lake. Mostly moderately technical alpine singletrack, several variants (the La Perche line is the classic), then forest trails through Caux and Glion back to Montreux. Exposed and rocky up top - not a beginner run, and not much fun in the wet.<br/><br/><b>Rain sensitivity</b><br/>Rain-sensitive: steep forest and rocky upper trail become greasy after rain; choose a drier day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Montreux > Rochers-de-Naye return is 70 CHF full fare / 35 CHF with a half-fare card. A cheaper ascent-only day ticket for bikers and paragliders (around 39 CHF) has been offered in past seasons. Bike capacity on the rack train is genuinely limited - call MVR ahead rather than turning up with three mates.<br/><br/><p class="warn">⚠️ Only ride on single tracks that are marked for biking, or carrosable, as this is Vaud canton.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 May; closed from 1 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h25</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.mob.ch/en/pages/rochers-de-naye">MOB Rochers-de-Naye</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
