  <Placemark>
    <name>Les 7 Laux - Prapoutel (Belledonne) [21.50 EUR online]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Chamois - top of the chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The other side of the Belledonne from Chamrousse, and the rowdier of the two. A dense set of numbered descents - Or'Anjina, Bel'Dina, Jasse and Cortillets for flow, Bloody Roots and Bloody Rock for the rough stuff, Mini Shore and Chevre Shore for woodwork. Steep, rooty and often damp under the trees, with a long run-out all the way to Froges in the valley if you want the full 1100 m.<br/><br/><b>Rain sensitivity</b><br/>Rain-sensitive: rooty, shaded forest terrain stays damp and becomes slippery quickly after rain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Day pass 21.50 EUR online, 23.50 EUR at the window; 4 hours 18 EUR, two days 37.50 EUR, six days 67 EUR. Lifts run 4 July to 30 August 2026, and the Bouquetins and Chamois chairlifts alternate rather than both running every day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 4 July; closed from 31 August (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Grenoble</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.les7laux.com/en/summer/bike-park/">Les 7 Laux</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>6.018802,45.247142,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>sept-laux</value></Data>
