  <Placemark>
    <name>Alpe d'Huez (Grandes Rousses) [25 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Pic Blanc 3300 m - top station of the DMC cable car</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Enormous: 45 routes over roughly 300 km of marked trail and 2610 m of vertical from the Pic Blanc at 3330 m down to 1450 m. Alpe d'Huez is the venue of Megavalanche, the iconic mass start race that launches riders together from the Pic Blanc glacier into a marathon descent to Allemond. The built lines around the resort cover everything - Marmotland and Easy Rider for beginners, the Rif Nel flow trail and Central Park for jumps, Hot Road and Run DMC when you want speed. Above them sits a high-alpine descent that is genuinely one of the longest in Europe.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>MTB day pass 25 EUR adult, 21.50 EUR child, 21.50 EUR each on a family pass, 7.50 EUR over 72. Season 27 June - 30 August 2026, with a pre-opening on the weekend of 27-28 June.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 31 August (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Grenoble</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://skipass.alpedhuez.com/hiver/en/bike-park/">Alpe d'Huez</a> and <a href="https://www.ucc-sportevent.com/en/megavalanche-alpe-dhuez-en/">Megavalanche</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>6.127280,45.125050,0</coordinates></Point>
