  <Placemark>
    <name>Murren (Lauterbrunnen) [Jungfrau lifts, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Murren - car-free village and lift hub</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Murren Bike, SuisseMobile route 450: a high balcony traverse and descent under the Eiger, Monch and Jungfrau, which is as good a backdrop as riding gets. More mountain route than bike park - alp tracks, some singletrack, and a long drop back to the Lauterbrunnen valley floor. Go for the setting rather than the trail features.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Reached by cable car and mountain railway from Lauterbrunnen - Murren has no road, so everything comes up by lift. Bike carriage is possible but capacity is tight and the 2026 fares are not confirmed here; check jungfrau.ch first.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 19 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 06:00-23:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~3h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://muerren.swiss/en/experiences/summer/biking/">Murren tourism</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
