  <Placemark>
    <name>Grindelwald - First [Firstbahn, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>First 2168 m - top of the Firstbahn</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>15 km and 1100 m of descent from First back to Grindelwald on natural paths and tracks, under the north face of the Eiger the whole way. Not a built bike park - this is a big mountain descent with a gondola instead of a climb, and it splits naturally at Bort if you want a shorter day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Firstbahn gondola. Bike carriage and the exact 2026 fare are not confirmed here - check jungfrau.ch. Adventure packages bundling unlimited gondola use with activities are usually the better value if you are staying.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 26 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-17:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~3h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.jungfrau.ch/en-gb/grindelwaldfirst/">Grindelwald-First</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>8.052960,46.661377,0</coordinates></Point>
