  <Placemark>
    <name>Zermatt - Sunnegga [~55 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sunnegga 2285 m - top of the Sunnegga Express funicular</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Zermatt wraps a bike park in four-thousand-metre scenery. The Sunnegga-Trail (blue) is a 7 km flow descent all the way to town; the Riffelberg Trail is a 6.5 km natural enduro line with Matterhorn views the whole way down. The Moos-Trail and short connectors around the Sunnegga-Blauherd mid-station give you extra variety before the final drop to the village. Most routes funnel back to the high street, so the apres-ride pizza is 30 seconds from the bottom.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Sunnegga Express (underground funicular) carries bikes inside the cabin. Day bike pass around 55 CHF - price not verified here; check zermatt.ch before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 19 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.zermatt.ch/en/bike">Zermatt</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>7.770060,46.017290,0</coordinates></Point>
