  <Placemark>
    <name>La Forclaz - Le Tsaté (Val d'Hérens) [small t-bar]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Le Tsaté 2200 m - top of the t-bar</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A tiny, old-school bike spot on a south-facing slope above Evolène. Two surface lifts - a platter and a t-bar - drag you and your bike up to just above 2200 m, and you drop back through larch forest and open pasture on natural, unsurfaced singletrack. No bike park features, no crowd, just a quiet local run with views of the Dent Blanche and the Val d'Hérens. The restaurant at the bottom does a solid croûte au fromage.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Small t-bar (téléski du Tsaté) and platter lift - bikes tag along on a hook. Day pass around 15-20 CHF; price not verified here. Check with the Evolène tourist office before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 May; closed from 1 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.evolene-region.ch/">Evolène Région Tourisme</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
