  <Placemark>
    <name>Menton - St Agnes - Col de la Madone - Peille [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sainte-Agnes 800 m - pedal-access trail hub above Menton</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A broad natural enduro area linking Sainte-Agnes, Castillon, Col de la Madone, Peille and Gorbio. Historic paths and technical singletrack can be linked into longer rides, including the red GR51 descent from Sainte-Agnes to Monti and the black Ravin du Rank from Col de la Madone toward Gorbio. The Ravin drops about 550 m over 2.8 km and is graded T5 / E2, with loose limestone, stone steps and exposed sections.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no trail fee. Climb by road from Menton, Sainte-Agnes, Gorbio or Peille; shuttling by car is possible for some lines.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Ravin du Rank is T5 and exposed. Scout the step sections before committing.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round in a typical year; check weather, wildfire restrictions and local trail access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Menton</td><td>Bike</td><td>~1 h climb</td></tr><tr><td>Nice</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://vttour.fr/sentiers/83">VTTour Ravin du Rank</a>, <a href="https://vttour.fr/sentiers/137">VTTour Sainte-Agnes - Monti</a>, and the linked OpenStreetMap trail geometries (ODbL). Routes and access can change; verify locally.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
