  <Placemark>
    <name>Val di Sole Bike Park (Daolasa, Trentino) [46 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Val Mastellina 2040 m - top of the Daolasa gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The World Cup venue, and host of the 2026 World Championships. Four marked runs plus a four-cross track share 550 m of vertical: White Wolf is the blue, Golden Eagle and Wild Grizzly the reds, and Black Snake the black - a downhill course cut by Pippo Marani and widely counted among the steepest and most technical on the circuit. Golden Eagle was rebuilt for 2026 and Black Snake gained a new diagonal and counter-slope section.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The 8-seat Daolasa - Val Mastellina gondola runs from Commezzadura in the valley floor. Bike day pass 46 EUR adult, 32 EUR junior, 23 EUR child. Open 27 June to 13 September 2026. The park joined the Gravity Card circuit in 2026, so that pass works here too.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 14 September (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Trento</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Milan</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.valdisolebikeland.com/en/bike-parks">Val di Sole Bikeland</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
