  <Placemark>
    <name>Machairas - Lythrodontas (Cyprus) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Machairas Forest mountain-bike hub from Lythrodontas</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Cyprus's strongest documented mountain-bike area combines long rough dirt tracks, pine forest, sudden technical descents and substantial climbing around Kionia, Machairas Monastery and Mantra tou Kampiou. The area hosts major MTB races, but it is a natural route network rather than a gravity park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Free and pedal-accessed; no lift. The official 45 km circular route gains about 890 m and is rated very difficult. Guided e-MTB trips are available locally.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 October; closed from 01 June (best cooler-season window; access may be possible year-round).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Summer heat and fire restrictions can affect forest access; check locally.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Nicosia</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Larnaca</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.visitcyprus.com/discover-cyprus/rural/cycling-rural/lythrodontas-circular-cycling-route/">Visit Cyprus circular route</a> and the <a href="https://www.visitcyprus.com/discover-cyprus/nature/cycling/lefkosia-2-lythrodontas-kionia-machairas-monastery-lythrodontas-cycling-route/">Machairas route guide</a>. Follow current forestry rules.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>33.298047,34.951352,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>machairas-lythrodontas</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>expert natural no-lift enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>10-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>06-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Troodos Mountain Bike Routes (Cyprus) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Highland riding around Troodos Square and Mount Olympus</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Troodos cycling network mixes paved connectors, rough mining and forest roads, and natural mountain descents through pine forest and exposed ophiolite geology. It is best treated as adventure/enduro touring rather than a signed downhill park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No documented summer bike uplift. Ride from Troodos Square or build pedal/shuttle routes with a local guide; winter ski lifts should not be assumed to carry bikes.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 April; closed from 01 December (typical snow-free riding window).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Check forestry closures, heat, fire risk and route legality before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Limassol</td><td>Car</td><td>~55 min</td></tr><tr><td>Nicosia</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.troodosgeopark.com/en">Troodos UNESCO Global Geopark</a> and the official <a href="https://www.visitcyprus.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Cycling-WEB-ONLY.pdf">Visit Cyprus cycling guide</a>. Confirm current access locally.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>32.880740,34.922037,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>troodos-cycling</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert natural no-lift enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>04-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>12-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Mzaar Mountain Resort MTB (Lebanon) [no bike lift documented]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Summer mountain-bike trails at Mzaar Kfardebian</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Lebanon's largest mountain resort advertises summer MTB trails designed for speed, mountain exploration and full-day riding. Expect open limestone terrain, high ridges and natural resort tracks rather than a fully documented modern downhill park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Book the resort's MTB activity or arrange local support. Summer bicycle carriage on the ski lifts could not be verified, so plan on pedal or vehicle-assisted access rather than assuming uplift.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 May; closed from 01 December (typical snow-free window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical activity hours; booking, access and local conditions must be confirmed directly.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Beirut</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Faraya</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.mzaarresort.com/activity/mtb-trail">Mzaar Mountain Resort</a>. Confirm the precise route, booking and access before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>35.847454,33.984282,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>mzaar-mtb</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert natural no-lift enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>05-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>12-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Chouf - Barouk Cedar Reserve MTB (Lebanon) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Natural mountain riding around Barouk and the Chouf</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Chouf is one of Lebanon's best-known mountain-bike regions, with long climbs and descents on rough tracks between Barouk, Maasser el Chouf, cedar forest and exposed Mount Lebanon ridges. The attraction is backcountry scenery and endurance-oriented natural riding, not purpose-built gravity trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal the routes or arrange guide and vehicle support. The cedar reserve is protected: bicycles may be restricted to designated roads and routes, so confirm the exact itinerary with reserve staff.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 May; closed from 01 December (typical snow-free window).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Reserve hours, security conditions, snow and fire restrictions can change.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Beirut</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Barouk</td><td>Bike</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: official Lebanon tourism cycling guidance and the <a href="https://shoufcedar.org/">Shouf Biosphere Reserve</a>. Confirm bicycle permissions and current local conditions before riding.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>35.702272,33.705273,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>chouf-barouk</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>expert natural no-lift enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>05-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>12-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
