    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>mavrovo</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert natural no-lift enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>04-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>12-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Peja - Rugova and Accursed Mountains (Kosovo) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Natural enduro and adventure riding from Rugova Canyon</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Kosovo's best-documented mountain-bike destination links Peja, Rugova Canyon and the Accursed Mountains. Mapped routes deliver more than 1700 m of vertical across rocky mule paths, forest singletrack, high pasture and cross-border adventure terrain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No verified mechanical uplift. Pedal from Peja or arrange local guide and vehicle support. Border-crossing and protected-area routes may require permissions, so confirm the exact itinerary.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 May; closed from 01 November (typical snow-free window).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Check weather, border requirements and local trail access.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Peja</td><td>Bike / shuttle</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Pristina</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://pejatourism.org/cycling/">Peja Tourism</a> and its outdoor-activity publications. Confirm routes and permissions locally.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>20.208657,42.663523,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>peja-rugova</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>expert natural no-lift enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>05-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>11-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Mottolino Bike Park (Livigno) [from 29.50 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mottolino gondola to 2400 m above Livigno</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of Italy's benchmark gravity parks, with downhill race tracks, accessible flow, North Shore woodwork, a dedicated jump area, drops and large freeride features. It hosted the 2005 MTB World Championships and remains Livigno's harder, park-focused sector.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Mottolino gondola carries bikes. Bike passes start from 29.50 EUR; rentals, workshop and coaching are at the base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 13 June; closed from 28 September (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Published 2026 hours; check live trail status.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Livigno centre</td><td>Bike / bus</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>St Moritz</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.mottolino.com/en/summer/bike-park/">Mottolino</a>. Prices and operations can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>10.162912,46.526810,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>mottolino</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-13</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-28</value></Data><Data name="price_day"><value>29.50 EUR</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Carosello 3000 Mountain Park (Livigno) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Carosello gondola - Livigno's flow and enduro sector</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The western side of Livigno emphasizes long, flowing mountain-bike trails, high-alpine enduro and natural singletrack rather than pure DH. Rolling blue progression, fast red flow and big panoramic descents link Carosello, Costaccia and the Sitas area.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Carosello 3000 and connecting summer lifts carry bikes. Check Livigno for the current area or combined bike pass.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 20 June; closed from 27 September (typical 2026 summer window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical lift hours; verify the operating calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Livigno centre</td><td>Bike / bus</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.carosello3000.com/it/">Carosello 3000</a> and <a href="https://www.livigno.eu/en/">Livigno Tourism</a>. Verify current lifts and trails.</i>]]></description>
