  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Mook (Netherlands) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Purpose-built gravity playground in the Mookerheide woods</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A compact but varied Dutch progression park connected to the Nijmegen-area MTB routes. Its short hand-built lines cover flow, berms, tables, drops and technical features, with options for developing riders and harder lines for experienced jumpers.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Free and pedal-accessed; push or ride back up between short laps. No mechanical uplift.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 January; closed from 01 January (normally year-round).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Do not ride during closures or when wet conditions would damage the trails.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Nijmegen</td><td>Bike / train + bike</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://bike-park-mook.nl/">Bikepark Mook</a>. Check the park's current trail status and rules.</i>]]></description>
