  <Placemark>
    <name>The Mother Bikepark Winterberg (Germany) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Three uplifts serving Germany's largest gravity park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A dense network of downhill, freeride, jump and flow lines makes Winterberg the reference park in northern Germany. It spans beginner progression trails through technical DH and large-feature freeride terrain, with rental and coaching at the base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Three lifts serve the park. Ticket prices vary by product and date; the official shop publishes current rates. Multi-day tickets shared with Willingen are available.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 24 April; closed from 09 November (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:30 April-September; 09:30-16:30 October-November<br/><small>Published 2026 hours; individual lifts and trails may close.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Dortmund</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr><tr><td>Winterberg station</td><td>Bike</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.bike-park-winterberg.de/opening-hours">Bikepark Winterberg</a>. Check live lift, trail and ticket information.</i>]]></description>
