  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Todtnau (Black Forest, Germany) [chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Hasenhorn 1026 m - Germany's oldest bike park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Todtnau is a compact expert-oriented Black Forest classic. Its race-bred downhill is steep, rough and technical, while Wildride and the jump line add faster, more shaped alternatives across roughly 360 m of vertical.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Hasenhorn chairlift carries riders and bikes from Todtnau. Check the operator for the current bike ticket price.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 April; closed from 03 November (typical season; check current dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:30<br/><small>Typical published day hours; weather and maintenance can affect operations.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Freiburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Basel</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.hochschwarzwald.de/attraktionen/bike-park-todtnau-69307d3f50">Hochschwarzwald Tourism</a> and <a href="https://www1.bwegt.de/land-und-leute/das-land-erleben/ausflugsziele/detail/bike-park-todtnau/bike-park-todtnau/69e8f606-d6b2-4054-8bbb-91f9eceb4263">bwegt</a>. Verify lift and trail status.</i>]]></description>
