  <Placemark>
    <name>Silkeborg BikePark (Denmark) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Progressive municipal jump and flow park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Silkeborg's MTB playground uses ski-style colour grading. A rollable green flow line leads toward blue and red jump progression, while the black jump line has four large, steep tables and closely spaced expert features.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Free and pedal- or push-accessed; no lift. Walk unfamiliar jump lines before riding.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 January; closed from 01 January (normally year-round).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Avoid riding when wet or when local closures are posted.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Silkeborg station</td><td>Bike</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Aarhus</td><td>Train + bike</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.visitdenmark.com/denmark/plan-your-trip/silkeborg-bike-park-gdk1112065">VisitDenmark / VisitAarhus</a>. Check local conditions before riding.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>9.573603,56.191598,0</coordinates></Point>
