  <Placemark>
    <name>Fujimi Panorama (Nagano, Japan) [5500 JPY]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Summit 1780 m - top of the Suzuran gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Japan's best-known downhill hill, on the flank of the Yatsugatake with the Southern Alps across the valley. Courses run from a wide beginner flow line to steep, rooty and rutted expert tracks; the longest links 8 km of trail for 730 m of descent, which makes for laps that punish arms rather than legs. A separate gentle skill-improvement area sits at the base for anyone starting out.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Suzuran gondola lifts riders and bikes from 1055 m to the 1780 m summit in around 10 minutes; two pair lifts serve the lower courses. One-day gondola and lift pass 5500 JPY adult, 2800 JPY child; the skill area alone is 2500 JPY. The 2026 season runs 24 April to 15 November.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 24 April; closed from 16 November (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tokyo</td><td>Train + shuttle</td><td>~3h00</td></tr><tr><td>Fujimi station</td><td>Shuttle</td><td>~10 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.fujimipanorama.com/mtb/">Fujimi Panorama</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
