  <Placemark>
    <name>Saalbach Hinterglemm - Schattberg (Salzburg) [39 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Schattberg Ost 2010 m - top of the Schattberg X-Press</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The other half of the Epic Bikepark, and the one that rewards riding all day rather than lapping one line. Over 36 km of park trail plus a dozen singletracks spread across both sides of a long valley, so you can cross the whole thing on lifts. The Hacklbergtrail from the Schattberg is the classic: 6 km and 600 m of descent of natural, flowing singletrack rather than berms. The Reiterkogel side holds the built lines - Blue Line, X-Line, Pro Line - and 18 km of new trail opened at Schoenleiten for 2026.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Schattberg X-Press lifts bikes in two sections out of Saalbach at 990 m; a dozen other lifts carry bikes across the valley. Day pass 39 EUR adult, cheaper booked online, and free discounts apply with a JOKER CARD from local accommodation. The Leogang season pass is valid here.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 May; closed from 27 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Salzburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.saalbach.com/en/summer/mountain-biking">Saalbach</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
