  <Placemark>
    <name>Bike Republic Soelden (Oetztal, Tirol) [39 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Giggijoch 2270 m - top of the Giggijochbahn</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>High-alpine riding above the tree line, which almost nowhere else on this map offers on a lift ticket. 33 shaped lines over 42 km, and more than 70 km once the singletracks and enduro routes are counted. The Teaere Line is the flagship flow descent; the Gahe Line is the one people come back with stories about. Two separate lift systems, Giggijoch and Gaislachkogl, open different halves of the mountain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Giggijochbahn and Gaislachkoglbahn gondolas both take bikes and both sell tickets. Day pass 39 EUR adult, 28 EUR from 11:30. Being at 2270 m, the season is short and weather-dependent - check the lift status before driving up the Oetztal.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 12 June; closed from 5 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Innsbruck</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://bikerepublic.soelden.com/">Bike Republic Solden</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
