  <Placemark>
    <name>Flims Laax Falera - Crap Sogn Gion (Graubunden) [from 49 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Crap Sogn Gion 2215 m - top of the LAAX cable car</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of the best-built trail networks in Switzerland, and the home of the Runca Trail: 7.6 km and 740 m of descent of flow, widely rated the finest flow line in the country. The Never End Trail adds a long natural descent back towards Flims, and the mini pipe and freestyle area at Crap Sogn Gion are the summer half of the resort's park-and-pipe reputation.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The LAAX cable car and the Arena Express from Flims both carry bikes to Crap Sogn Gion. Bike day passes start around 49 CHF for an adult; rates vary by date, so book online.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 26 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Zurich</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr><tr><td>Chur</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.flimslaax.com/en/biking">Flims Laax</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
