  <Placemark>
    <name>Braunwald (Glarus) [gondola, bike free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Seblengrat 1890 m - top of the Grotzenbüel-Seblengrat chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A car-free village above Linthal with four lifts that carry bikes for free. Multiple MTB and e-bike routes traverse the sunny Glarus terrace with views into the Todi massif. The riding is XC and trail on alpine and forest paths, with bike guides available locally.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Braunwaldbahn funicular from Linthal, then the Hüttenberg-Grotzenbüel gondola and Gumen mixed lift to the high terrain. Bike transport is free on all lifts. Pay only the passenger ticket.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from June; closed from October (estimated summer lift window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check Sportbahnen Braunwald summer timetable.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Zurich</td><td>Train + funicular</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Linthal</td><td>Funicular</td><td>~7 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.braunwald.ch/de/sommer/bike-e-bike">Braunwald tourism</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl>
