  <Placemark>
    <name>SilverStar Bike Park (British Columbia) [84 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Silver Star summit 1885 m - top of the Summit Express gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Canada's second-largest bike park, and the one riders name when they have had enough of Whistler's crowds. Over 69 km of park trail inside a 139 km network, more than 870 berms, and a spread that runs from mellow green flow to double-black tech. The Comet Six Pack is the biggest mountain-bike lift in the country, 480 m of vertical in under eight minutes. Dry Okanagan dirt, which rides fast.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Summit Express gondola and the Comet Six Pack from the village at 1600 m. Adult day ticket 84 CAD.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 21 June; closed from 15 September (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Kelowna</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Vancouver</td><td>Car</td><td>~4h45</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.skisilverstar.com/summer/bike-park">SilverStar</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
