  <Placemark>
    <name>Mont-Tremblant (Quebec) [lift ticket, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Summit 875 m - top of the Telecabine Express</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The biggest gravity operation in eastern Canada after Bromont, and the one with the most vertical: 610 m from the summit to the pedestrian village, on Laurentian granite that stays technical in the wet. The network mixes machine-built flow on the lower mountain with rooty, rocky natural lines up top, and the cross-country trails around Lac Tremblant run for kilometres.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Telecabine Express gondola from the village at 260 m. Summer bike ticket prices are sold through the resort and we could not confirm a 2026 adult rate; check tremblant.ca.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 24 May; closed from 13 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Montreal</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr><tr><td>Ottawa</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.tremblant.ca/things-to-do/activities/mountain-biking">Tremblant</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
