  <Placemark>
    <name>Fujiten Resort (Yamanashi) [lift pass, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Top station 1450 m - on the north flank of Mount Fuji</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A ski hill that turns over to mountain bikes for the green season, with courses laid out by the professional freerider Daiki Takahashi. The range is unusually wide for a small hill: open piste lines that a first-timer can roll down, through to technical built sections that will hold an expert's attention. Mount Fuji is directly above you, which no other park on this map can offer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Chairlifts carry riders and bikes from the base at 1295 m. The resort publishes its green-season lift rates seasonally and we could not confirm a 2026 figure, so check fujiten.net before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 May; closed from 31 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tokyo</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr><tr><td>Kawaguchiko</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.fujiten.net/mtb/">Fujiten</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
