  <Placemark>
    <name>Thredbo (New South Wales, AU) [season 759 AUD; day rate unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kosciuszko Express top 1930 m - the gravity hub</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Australia's only lift-accessed mountain-bike park, and it carries the whole country's gravity scene on its own. The Kosciuszko Express serves the long descents, the Cannonball Downhill among them, while the Merritts Gondola opens the flow and all-mountain trails lower down. Grades run from green through to the race lines used by the Cannonball Festival every February. Dry, dusty granite country above the treeline, and nothing else like it within several thousand kilometres.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Kosciuszko Express chairlift and the Merritts Gondola both carry bikes from the village at 1370 m. The 2026/27 Gravity Pass starts at 759 AUD for the season; we could not confirm a single-day rate, so check thredbo.com.au. Note this is a southern-hemisphere season - it runs while the Alps are shut.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 21 November; closed from 27 April (published dates). 2026/27 season: 21 November 2026 to 26 April 2027.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Canberra</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr><tr><td>Sydney</td><td>Car</td><td>~5h30</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.thredbo.com.au/activities/biking/">Thredbo</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
