  <Placemark>
    <name>Oaxaca - Sierra Norte / Ixtepeji (MX) [shuttle, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Santa Catarina Ixtepeji 2355 m - the shuttle village</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Where enduro started in Mexico, and still the best riding in the country. The Ixtepeji forest, 45 minutes north of Oaxaca City, holds long descents through semi-wet pine and oak between roughly 2800 m and 3240 m on the ridge above, dropping thousands of metres towards the valley. Dry rocky lines, loamy forest lines, and enough of them that operators run multi-day trips without repeating.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift: pickups shuttle riders to the ridge, which is how essentially all Mexican gravity riding works. The trails cross communal Zapotec land, so go with one of the Oaxaca operators rather than turning up alone - it is also how the communities get paid. Costs are per-tour, not per-day, so no pass price here.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 November; closed from 15 June (typical window; check the operator and conditions). The summer rains are the off season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Oaxaca City</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://sierranorte.org.mx/">Sierra Norte Expediciones</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
