  <Placemark>
    <name>Peyragudes-Loudenvielle Bike Park (Pyrenees) [33 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Peyragudes 2400 m to Loudenvielle 950 m - lift-served Pyrenean enduro</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Twenty marked green-to-black downhill and enduro trails sit inside the Louron valley's much larger 420 km riding network. The full mountain combines maintained park lines, long natural enduro descents and World Cup terrain, with exceptional vertical back to the lake at Loudenvielle.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Skyvall carries bikes from Loudenvielle to 1600 m, then the Privilege chairlift reaches the high trail starts. The 2026 full-area adult day pass starts at 33 EUR; a station-only or Skyvall-only pass starts at 28 EUR.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 8 May; closed from 19 October (published 2026 span). May, June, September and October are mostly weekends and holidays; daily operation is from 4 July through 30 August, and the upper chairlifts run on selected days.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tarbes</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h10</td></tr><tr><td>Toulouse</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h50</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.n-py.com/fr/peyragudes/bike-park">official N'PY bike park page</a>; verify which lifts operate on your date.</i>]]></description>
