  <Placemark>
    <name>Les Angles Bike Park (Pyrenees) [24.50 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Roc d'Aude sector above Les Angles - 500 m of lift-served vertical</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>About 30 km of purpose-built riding across nine descents and five difficulty levels. Long blue and red marathon lines drop through pine forest, while black tracks, jumps, a North Shore line and the separate Flow Zone cover more committed riding and skill progression.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The village gondola serves the park. The published adult day pass starts at 24.50 EUR, with four-hour and multi-day options also available.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 31 August (published 2026 dates). The park operates daily in the main window, subject to weather and the Tour de France closure on 6 July 2026.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Perpignan</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Barcelona</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://lesangles.com/evenement/ouverture-bike-park-les-angles/">Les Angles 2026 opening notice</a> and official ticket shop; check lift status.</i>]]></description>
