  <Placemark>
    <name>Innerleithen and Golfie (Scotland, UK) [optional shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Traquair and Caberston forests - technical Tweed Valley enduro</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Innerleithen's four formal downhill tracks drop steeply from Plora Rig, while the adjacent Golfie in Caberston Forest is famous for demanding natural enduro trails. Expect roots, mud, rock, steep chutes and limited easy options; this is primarily an expert destination.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Pedal and push-up access is always the baseline. Adrenalin Uplift runs a bookable shuttle to the formal downhill hill when available; current prices and dates depend on its calendar.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Normally rideable year-round, subject to storm damage, forestry operations, trail maintenance and shuttle availability.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Edinburgh</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h10</td></tr><tr><td>Glentress</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://forestryandland.gov.scot/visit/destinations/innerleithen/bike">Forestry and Land Scotland</a>; clean bikes to limit forest disease and obey closures.</i>]]></description>
