  <Placemark>
    <name>Mona YongPyong MTB Park (Pyeongchang, KR) [gondola, public price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Balwangsan at Mona YongPyong - South Korea's 2026 UCI World Cup gravity venue</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Purpose-built downhill and cross-country race terrain on the steep forested slopes of Balwangsan. Mona YongPyong hosted Asia's first UCI Mountain Bike World Series round in May 2026, with a full downhill course, technical natural sections and a dedicated finish bowl. This is serious race terrain rather than a broad beginner holiday network.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The resort gondola carried bikes from the main venue to the downhill start and the Rainbow chairlift returned accredited riders during the 2026 World Cup. A normal public bike-uplift price and calendar were not verified, so contact the resort before travelling outside an announced MTB event.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 May; closed from 1 October (estimated snow-free riding window). Public trail and uplift access may be limited to scheduled events even inside this period.<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Seoul</td><td>Car / intercity bus</td><td>~2h30</td></tr><tr><td>Gangneung</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.czechcyclingfederation.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Event_Guide_-_South_Korea_V1.pdf">2026 UCI event guide</a> and <a href="https://www.yongpyong.co.kr/eng/index.do">official Mona YongPyong site</a>; confirm public MTB access.</i>]]></description>
