  <Placemark>
    <name>Manizales / Neira Coffee Trails (CO) [shuttle, price unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Neira and the cloud-forest ridges above Manizales</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>World-class natural enduro in Colombia's coffee country: long, raw descents mix loam, slick roots, rock, tight jungle turns and plantation paths. The area has hosted Enduro World Series racing, but it is a riding zone rather than a signed bike park; a local guide is strongly recommended.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Commercial guides use 4x4 or traditional chiva-style road shuttles. There is no public lift or standard day-pass price, and trail access can cross private farms.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; December-March and July-August are usually drier. Avoid saturated trails and confirm landslide and private-land access locally.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Manizales</td><td>Guide shuttle</td><td>~35 min to Neira</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://colombia.travel/en/colombia-in-expodubai/trails-del-cafe">Colombia Travel: Trails del Cafe</a> and <a href="https://colombiamountainbiking.com/about/">Colombia MTB</a>.</i>]]></description>
