  <Placemark>
    <name>San Gil / Chicamocha Mule Trails (CO) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>San Gil and Chicamocha Canyon - rocky backcountry enduro</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Historic mule tracks, dry canyon paths and rough mountain roads create long, rocky adventure rides around San Gil and the Chicamocha rim. This is exposed backcountry riding, not a maintained trail centre; route-finding, heat and water management matter more than bike-park features.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No bike lift. Pedal point-to-point, arrange a local vehicle, or book a guide. Confirm access across villages and private land.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; December-March is typically driest. Avoid the hottest part of the day and check storm conditions in the canyon.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bucaramanga</td><td>Car / bus</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Indicative regional adventure-riding pin; use a local guide and verify the chosen route.</i><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://colombia.travel/en/san-gil">Colombia Travel</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
