  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Beijing Xishan / Xiangshan MTB Trails (CN) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Unofficial singletrack in the Western Hills above Beijing</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A network of unofficial singletrack, fireroad climbs and DIY technical descents through the forested Western Hills (Xishan / Xiangshan / Miaofengshan) above Haidian District. Trails range from easy fireroads to steep expert lines with rock gardens. This is a local-community riding zone, not a sanctioned or signed trail network.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. All riding is pedal-up or shuttle via local group arrangements. No trail pass required. Respect park access rules and avoid hiking paths where cycling is prohibited.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best March-May and September-November. Summer is hot and humid; winter is cold but dry and rideable.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Central Beijing</td><td>Metro + bike</td><td>~45 min to trailhead</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Indicative urban trail-zone pin. No mapped or sanctioned MTB network exists; riding is driven by local WeChat-group knowledge and word of mouth. Confirm current access with local riders before travelling.</i><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: local Beijing riding community reports. Check current trail access and park restrictions.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>116.187,39.994,0</coordinates></Point>
