  <Placemark>
    <name>Lao Wai Trails / Dadu Trail House (Taichung, TW) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Expat-built XC and enduro network above Taichung</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A network of flow and XC trails on Dadu Mountain, built and maintained by the expat MTB community. The Dadu Trail House bar, cafe and bike-rental shop is the local hub, with e-bikes available. Trails are shared-use, unsigned and known by local word of mouth.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal up from the urban fringe or start at the Dadu Trail House for local knowledge and rentals.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; avoid typhoon rains (Jul-Sep) and the hottest summer afternoons.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Central Taichung</td><td>Bike / taxi</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Community trail network; no formal trail map. Start at Dadu Trail House for current conditions and guidance.</i><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: local rider reports and <a href="https://ziraneffect.com/">Ziran Effect blog</a>.</i>]]></description>
