  <Placemark>
    <name>Kenting MTB Trails (Pingtung, TW) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Coastal tropical singletrack in southern Taiwan</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Singletrack, downhill sections and jump/drop playgrounds around Dajianshr Mountain inside Kenting National Park. Open coastal terrain with ocean views makes this Taiwan's most scenic trail zone, but heat, sun exposure and typhoon risk require planning.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal from the park access roads. A local guide (@accompany_bike_studio) offers supported rides.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; avoid typhoon season (Jul-Sep) when trails can be closed or washed out. Heat is intense in summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Kenting / Hengchun</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Kaohsiung</td><td>Car / bus</td><td>~2h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Natural trail riding inside a national park; respect all signage, park rules and weather closures.</i><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: local rider reports and <a href="https://ziraneffect.com/">Ziran Effect blog</a>.</i>]]></description>
