  <Placemark>
    <name>Blue River Provincial Park MTB (Yate, NC) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Red-dirt forest riding in Parc Provincial de la Riviere Bleue</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Six designated MTB routes sit within roughly 54 km of park tracks, crossing red earth, native forest, river scenery and the Perignon bridge area. The riding ranges from touring loops to longer backcountry outings rather than gravity laps.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No bike lift. Pedal from the park entrance or use the internal visitor shuttle where permitted; confirm reservations, bicycle transport and current entry fees before travel.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round Wednesday-Sunday, subject to weather, fire risk and provincial closures. <br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-16:00<br/><small>Published Wednesday-Sunday hours; check provincial notices and booking requirements.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Noumea</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.newcaledonia.travel/activities/preserved-nature/mountain-biking-and-cycling/">New Caledonia Tourism MTB guide</a> and the <a href="https://www.nouvellecaledonie.travel/destination/grand-sud/parc-provincial-de-la-riviere-bleue/">provincial park overview</a>.</i>]]></description>
