  <Placemark>
    <name>Pic Paradis (Saint Martin, MF) [access must be checked, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Steep tropical ridge riding around Saint Martin's highest point</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Natural tracks around the 424 m Pic Paradis ridge provide short, steep descents, rocky sections and broad views toward Marigot and Grand Case. The mapped riding is informal and overlaps hiking terrain; this is not a sanctioned bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal the steep access road or arrange a local vehicle drop where legal. Loterie Farm is private property and its marked trails are primarily for walking, so obtain permission and confirm the exact bicycle route locally.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best December-May during the drier season. Avoid tropical storms and wet clay; hurricane damage can alter access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Marigot</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Grand Case</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.visitstmaarten.com/nature-hiking/paradise-peak-pic-paradis/">official island tourism overview</a> and <a href="https://www.trailforks.com/region/saint-martin/">mapped local MTB activity</a>. Confirm access before riding.</i>]]></description>
