  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Foret de Montravail MTB (Martinique, MQ) [shared trails, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Accessible forest trail riding above Sainte-Luce</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A compact network of maintained forest tracks combines rolling climbs, roots and short natural descents. Martinique Tourism recommends Montravail for intermediate MTB riders, but the forest is shared with walkers and is not a gravity bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Free pedal access; no lift. Build loops from the forest parking areas and remain on routes where cycling is permitted.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round, with the most reliable conditions December-May. Rain makes roots and tropical clay extremely slippery.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sainte-Luce</td><td>Car / bike</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Fort-de-France</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.martinique.org/en/blog/activities-sports/mountain-biking-martinique">Martinique Tourism MTB guide</a>. Yield to walkers and respect current forestry notices.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
