  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Shymbulak Bike Park (Almaty, KZ) [uplift status unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>High-altitude resort terrain above Almaty</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Shymbulak's published resort rules define a downhill bike park with purpose-built natural and artificial features, using the steep ski terrain between roughly 2,200 and 3,180 m. However, the official 2026 summer programme does not currently list public MTB operation, so trail maintenance and access must be confirmed before travel.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Medeu-Shymbulak gondola and upper lifts operate for summer visitors, but 2026 bicycle carriage, bike-park uplift and prices are unverified. Do not assume a sightseeing ticket includes a bicycle.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Current bike-park operation is unverified. Contact Shymbulak before planning a riding day.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Potential summer operation from June through September; snow, maintenance and national-park restrictions apply. <br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-18:00<br/><small>Summer resort estimate only; bicycle uplift and bike-park operation must be confirmed.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Central Almaty</td><td>Bus/taxi + gondola</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://shymbulak.com/en/info/about/">official resort overview</a> and the <a href="https://storage.yandexcloud.kz/shymbulak/media-test/58b2111d00c198fd54a290b715e88372.pdf">published resort rules</a>.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>77.0802,43.1280,0</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>shymbulak-mtb</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>expert bike-park dh</value></Data>
