  <Placemark>
    <name>Sapa Valley MTB (Vietnam) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Rice-terrace and mountain-village riding in northern Vietnam</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Steep roads, buffalo tracks and mixed dirt paths descend through rice terraces and Hmong villages around Sapa and the Muong Hoa valley. The riding is scenic and culturally sensitive rather than park-built, ranging from accessible valley tours to technical wet singletrack.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Mountain-bike rental and guided tours are available in Sapa; use a local guide for village access, route finding and point-to-point vehicle support.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best in April-May and September-October. Summer is hot and wet; winter can be cold, foggy and occasionally icy at altitude.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sapa centre</td><td>Bike</td><td>Immediate</td></tr><tr><td>Hanoi</td><td>Bus / train + van</td><td>~5-8h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.vietnam.travel/places-to-go/northern-vietnam/sapa">Vietnam Tourism</a>. Ride respectfully through working farms and villages.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
