  <Placemark>
    <name>Virgin Freeride / Red Bull Rampage Zone [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Virgin Freeride / Red Bull Rampage Zone - Virgin, UT</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Flying Monkey is the documented public expert descent from the southern rim of Smith Mesa north of Virgin: 2.53 miles of narrow, steep and loose trail with sharp turns, jumps, unavoidable obstacles, sudden drop-offs and extreme exposure. It runs through the same broader red-desert freeride landscape used by Red Bull Rampage. Historic and current Rampage competition lines are separate, invitation-only event terrain; do not treat them as public trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal the Mesa Road / Flying Monkey access roads or arrange a vehicle drop where legal; the BLM recommends leaving vehicles before the access road becomes rough.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Flying Monkey is rated extremely difficult by the BLM. It has 20% or steeper grades, crumbling surfaces and places where a mistake could cause serious injury or death. There are no convenient places to stop or turn around.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best from mid-September to mid-May. Avoid wet clay, summer heat and active event or land-management closures.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Virgin</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>~15 min to Mesa Road</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.blm.gov/visit/flying-monkey-trail">BLM Flying Monkey trail description, access and safety guidance</a> and <a href="https://www.redbull.com/us-en/events/red-bull-rampage/">Red Bull Rampage event information</a>. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
