  <Placemark>
    <name>Maydena Bike Park (Tasmania, AU) [95 AUD uplift + mountain pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Australia's largest gravity bike park and Red Bull Hardline Tasmania venue</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>More than 85 gravity trails descend up to 820 vertical metres from the summit and midline shuttle drops. The network mixes long natural enduro lines, race-speed downhill, large jump and drop trails, plus skills areas; summit uplift is intended for intermediate to advanced riders.<br/><br/>
    <b>Red Bull Hardline</b><br/>Maydena has hosted the Southern Hemisphere edition of Red Bull Hardline since 2024, including the 7-8 February 2026 event. Its invitation-only Hardline course combines World Cup-level downhill with enormous jumps and drops. The course and eastern park sector close around the event and are not available for unsanctioned riding or spectating outside published event access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Truck uplift serves the summit and midline. The published 2026/27 adult summit uplift is 95 AUD; every rider also needs a separate Maydena Mountain Pass.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 3 October; closed from 29 June (published 2026/27 seasonal pattern, with varying weekly operating days).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Typical operating-day estimate; check the official calendar because uplift days and event closures vary.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Hobart</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Hobart Airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.maydenabike-park.com/pass-options/uplift-passes/">official uplift and trail information</a>, <a href="https://www.maydenabike-park.com/about/operating-hours/">operating calendar</a> and <a href="https://www.redbull.com/ca-en/events/red-bull-hardline-australia/red-bull-hardline-tasmania-faq">Red Bull Hardline Tasmania FAQ</a>. Book ahead and verify closures.</i>]]></description>
