  <Placemark>
    <name>Hellsend Dirt Compound (South Africa) [DarkFest venue, private]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Private freeride compound and home of DarkFest</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Hellsend on Vuurberg Wine Farm contains progressive dirt-jump lines, flow, expert downhill and the enormous invitation-only DarkFest jumps. DarkFest celebrated its tenth edition here in March 2026, with elite riders using gaps up to roughly 110 feet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Private venue with no normal public uplift or daily admission. Riding is limited to announced open sessions, bookings and sanctioned events.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Hellsend is private property and the DarkFest line is professional event terrain. Do not enter or ride without explicit permission.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>No public season. Check the operator for announced open sessions; the 2026 DarkFest event ran 14-22 March.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Stellenbosch</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Cape Town</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://thetrailscrew.com/hellsend-dirt-compound/">official Hellsend page</a> and <a href="https://www.monsterenergy.com/en-gb/bike/10-years-of-sending-it-darkfest-2026-announces-milestone-anniversary-and-heavyweight-rider-list/">DarkFest 2026 announcement</a>. Access is by permission only.</i>]]></description>
