  <Placemark>
    <name>Pachacamac / Pacha Trails (Lima, Peru) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lima's longstanding desert enduro and downhill network</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Loose, rocky and exposed desert singletrack in the hills above Pachacamac. Local classics include Prado, Terrucos, Jergon and other short, steep descents; Prado alone drops roughly 343 m with a black-diamond rating. Heat, dust, navigation and informal trail junctions make a local rider or guide valuable.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no unified trail fee. Pedal the desert roads and climbing lines or arrange a commercial guide and shuttle from Lima.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 January with no formal seasonal closure. Start early, carry water and avoid exceptional heat, fog or land closures.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Central Lima</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://mtbikeperu.com/en/mountain-biking-lima-pacha-trails/">local Pacha Trails guide</a> and <a href="https://www.trailforks.com/trails/prado-pachacamac/">Prado trail information</a>. Verify land access and current lines locally.</i>]]></description>
