  <Placemark>
    <name>Spirit Mountain / Manabao (Dominican Republic) [access unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Tropical enduro terrain in the mountains above Jarabacoa</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Spirit Mountain's coffee plantation and ecological reserve has hosted Dominican enduro racing and contains forest descents, flow and built gravity features. The wider Manabao and Jarabacoa area is the country's strongest mountain-riding region, with steep tropical terrain rather than resort lifts.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No public lift, regular opening calendar or current trail price could be verified. Contact Spirit Mountain or a Jarabacoa guide before travelling; do not assume plantation trails are open without permission.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 January with no formal MTB season, subject to private access and tropical rain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Jarabacoa</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Santo Domingo</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.dominicanenduroseries.com/about-us">Dominican Enduro Series</a> and <a href="https://www.godominicanrepublic.com/destinations/jarabacoa">official Jarabacoa tourism</a>. Confirm private access locally.</i>]]></description>
