  <Placemark>
    <name>Vinales Valley (Cuba) [no lift, guide recommended]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Adventure riding among the limestone mogotes of western Cuba</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Rural dirt roads, farm tracks and natural paths cross tobacco country between steep limestone towers. This is scenic backcountry trail riding rather than a maintained gravity park; route quality ranges from easy valley tracks to rough, muddy and technical connectors.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no unified trail fee. Hire a local guide and arrange a suitable bike in advance because rentals, parts and mapped legal singletrack are limited.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 November; closed from 1 May (drier-season indication). Tropical rain, farm activity and local restrictions can change access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Havana</td><td>Car / bus</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://visitcuba.com/adventure-travel/mountain-biking-guide/">Visit Cuba mountain-biking guide</a>. Verify routes and permissions with a local guide.</i>]]></description>
