  <Placemark>
    <name>LouzanPark (Lousa, Portugal) [shuttle service]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>World-class downhill and enduro in Serra da Lousa</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A large municipal mountain-bike center with downhill, enduro, cross-country and freeride routes on steep forested slopes above Lousa. Its technical natural tracks have hosted the UCI Downhill World Cup, European Championships and national enduro events, while easier marked routes broaden the network beyond the race lines.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>There is no mechanical lift. LouzanPark lists a transport service among its facilities, and local operators also run vehicle shuttles; availability and prices must be booked or confirmed before riding. Pedal access uses long forest roads.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 January with no fixed trail-season closure.<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>The municipal support center normally operates Monday-Friday 09:00-17:30. Trails and shuttle services have separate conditions; fire danger, forestry work and races can close sections.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Coimbra</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Porto</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://cm-lousa.pt/locais/louzan-park/?mp=57221">Lousa municipality LouzanPark page</a> and <a href="https://www.visitportugal.com/en/content/cycling">Visit Portugal cycling guide</a>. Confirm shuttle availability, fire restrictions and current trail status locally.</i>]]></description>
