  <Placemark>
    <name>Highland Mountain Bike Park (New Hampshire) [82 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>America's dedicated lift-served gravity mountain</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Opened as the world's first lift-accessed mountain dedicated entirely to biking, Highland is renowned for progressive downhill, huge jump lines, dirt jumps, skills zones and a world-class slopestyle course. Green learning terrain and coaching sit alongside race tracks and expert freeride lines such as NE Style and the Claymore competition terrain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The chairlift and Central Park surface lift serve the park. Published 2026 adult walk-up day passes are 68 USD midweek and 82 USD on weekends or holidays; season passes are also offered.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 23 April; closed from 16 November (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Core hours shown; Fridays run later in spring and summer, operating days reduce outside peak season, and late fall closes at 16:00. Check the detailed calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Boston</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Manchester, NH</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://highlandmountain.com/explore-highland/plan-your-visit/passes-rates-hours/">official 2026 passes, rates and hours</a>. Check the live conditions report and book ahead on busy dates.</i>]]></description>
