  <Placemark>
    <name>Blue Derby (Tasmania) [no lift, shuttle available]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>World-premier purpose-built Tasmanian singletrack</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Thirty-five purpose-built trails around the former mining town of Derby plus the Blue Tier wilderness routes. Famous Enduro World Series stages such as Detonate, Trouty, Kumma-Gutza and Shearpin mix enormous granite boulders, dense fern forest, sculpted flow and technical rock. The network spans genuine beginner loops through elite enduro terrain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No mechanical lift and the core trails are free to pedal. Multiple private operators sell uplift laps and longer shuttles for Blue Tier and Bay of Fires routes; prices and schedules vary, so reserve directly with an operator.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 January with no regular seasonal closure.<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>Rain can improve some granite-based trails but severe weather, maintenance, fire danger and events can close sections. Check the official trail status before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Launceston</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Hobart</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://ridebluederby.com.au/">official Blue Derby destination site</a> and its <a href="https://ridebluederby.com.au/trails">trail and uplift overview</a>. Check live trail status and book shuttles separately.</i>]]></description>
