  <Placemark>
    <name>Sarangkot / Pokhara Enduro Trails (Nepal) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Himalayan-view gravity above Pokhara</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Pokhara's best-known gravity riding links Sarangkot, Kahun Danda, Arba and the World Peace Pagoda hills. Expect long natural descents through subtropical forest, rock, dust, village paths and steep technical singletrack, with views across the Annapurna, Dhaulagiri and Manaslu ranges. Arba has been used for the Pokhara Enduro race.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Local operators offer guided rides, bike rental and vehicle support; a one-day guided Sarangkot product is available, while stronger riders can pedal roughly 800 m to the ridge. Book a local MTB specialist because trail entrances and permissions are not consistently signed.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 October; closed from 1 June (conservative dry-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>Winter mornings can be cold and misty. Avoid monsoon rain, landslides and saturated village trails from June through September.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Pokhara Lakeside</td><td>Guide vehicle / bike</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Pokhara Airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.nepalmountainbike.com/blog/epic-himalayan-enduro-mtb-trips-in-nepal-the-ultimate-adventure">Nepal MTB's Pokhara enduro overview</a> and its <a href="https://www.nepalmountainbike.com/mtb-tour/sarangkot-mountain-biking">Sarangkot ride page</a>. Use a current local guide and respect shared village paths.</i>]]></description>
