  <Placemark>
    <name>Nagarkot Enduro Trails (Nepal) [shuttle supported, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kathmandu Valley's established enduro zone</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Natural singletrack drops from the Nagarkot ridge through pine forest, terraces and villages toward the Kathmandu Valley. Guided Himalayan enduro itineraries use the area for repeated technical descents, mixing flow, roots, rock steps and tight local paths. It is a dispersed shared network rather than a signed park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Specialist operators run guided, shuttle-supported days from Kathmandu; self-guided route finding is difficult and can lead onto hiking paths or private land. Confirm the exact descent and vehicle arrangement when booking.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 October; closed from 1 June (conservative dry-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>Monsoon rain causes mud, erosion and landslide risk. Give way to walkers, villagers and livestock on every shared trail.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Kathmandu</td><td>Guide vehicle</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.wanderingwheels.ca/himalaya-enduro">shuttle-supported Himalaya Enduro itinerary</a> and <a href="https://himalayansingletrack.com/">Himalayan Single Track, a Kathmandu-based MTB operator</a>. Confirm current routes and permissions with a local guide.</i>]]></description>
