  <Placemark>
    <name>Doi Suthep-Pui Downhill (Chiang Mai, Thailand) [shuttle, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Northern Thailand's established jungle downhill hub</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A collection of technical natural descents on Doi Suthep and Doi Pui above Chiang Mai, ranging from guided introductory downhill to steep expert lines with roots, rock, ruts and slippery tropical soil. Trails cross national-park and sacred landscapes, are not consistently signed and have had access disputes, so current local guidance matters.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No mechanical lift. Trailhead publishes a private shuttle at 4800 THB per day for up to six experienced riders, excluding bikes, guide, park fees and insurance; guided downhill packages with bikes and protection are also available. The final shuttle lap must start by 15:30.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 November; closed from 1 April (preferred cool and dry-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-16:00<br/><small>Estimated riding window based on shuttle operation. Smoke season, extreme heat, monsoon mud and national-park closures can make trails unsuitable.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Chiang Mai Old City</td><td>Booked shuttle</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.trailhead.co.th/shuttle-service/">Trailhead shuttle service and price</a>, <a href="https://www.trailhead.co.th/tours/numb/">guided downhill tour</a> and <a href="https://www.trailhead.co.th/the-founding-of-the-chiang-mai-eco-cycling-association/">local trail-access context</a>. Confirm every trail with a reputable bicycle guide.</i>]]></description>
