  <Placemark>
    <name>Phnom Kulen MTB (Cambodia) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sacred sandstone mountain riding north of Siem Reap</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Phnom Kulen mixes red dirt, sandy jungle tracks, stone, village paths and a roughly 12 km guided downhill from the plateau toward the lowlands. The mountain hosted the mountain-bike events of the 2023 Southeast Asian Games, but ordinary visitor routes are shared and do not form a permanently signed gravity park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Guided tours use vehicle support from Siem Reap and combine plateau riding with the long descent. National-park admission and tour pricing vary; book a bicycle-specific guide who can confirm the legal route and transport.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Phnom Kulen is a national park and sacred cultural landscape. Stay on the guide-approved route, yield to walkers and residents, and never ride temple steps or archaeological features.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 November; closed from 1 May (drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>Monsoon rain makes sandstone, roots and river crossings hazardous. Heat is severe even in the dry season, so start early and carry ample water.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Siem Reap</td><td>Guide vehicle</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://camouflageadventures.com/tour-detail.html?name=Explore-kulen-mountain-bike-tour">guided Kulen mountain-bike and downhill route</a> and the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cycling_at_the_2023_SEA_Games">2023 SEA Games venue record</a>. Confirm park fees, route permission and conditions locally.</i>]]></description>
