  <Placemark>
    <name>Hlíðarfjall Bike Park (Iceland) [chairlifts]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Iceland's only lift-served bike park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Purpose-built downhill and enduro trails descend the open volcanic slopes above Akureyri, with connections toward Glerárdalur and Kjarnaskógur. The lower Fjarkinn chair serves the main park and selected summer weekends may also use Fjallkona, extending lift access above 1000 m. Expect exposed terrain, fast weather changes and a compact mix of flow and technical natural ground.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Fjarkinn is the regular bike-carrying summer chairlift; upper-lift operation is more limited. Tickets, operating days and which trails are open vary by season, so check the resort before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 10 July; closed from 8 September (typical published summer window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated daytime hours. Summer lifts commonly run only Thursday-Sunday and the upper chair on selected weekends. Wind, rain or residual snow can stop operations.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Akureyri</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.hlidarfjall.is/en/home">official Hlíðarfjall site</a> and <a href="https://www.visiticeland.com/service-provider/5ec7d096a90548233654DEA0">Visit Iceland's bike-park and summer-lift overview</a>. Confirm the current lift calendar and weather status.</i>]]></description>
