  <Placemark>
    <name>Sisimiut Backcountry Trails (Greenland) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Arctic dirt tracks and technical wilderness riding</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>East of Sisimiut, the road dissolves into a network of rocky dirt tracks suitable for mountain bikes, with options toward the valleys beneath Palasip Qaqqaa and the western end of the Arctic Circle Trail. Riding is raw, shared and unsigned rather than a managed bike park; terrain ranges from accessible dry tracks near town to hike-a-bike and serious remote travel.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift or permanent shuttle. Bikes may be borrowed or rented locally and guided town or wilderness outings are available. Use local advice before leaving the near-town tracks because there is no road connection, phone coverage or rapid rescue in the backcountry.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Do not assume marked hiking trails are rideable throughout. Protect fragile tundra, yield to walkers, avoid wet ground and turn back before terrain or river crossings exceed your expedition skills.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 July; closed from 15 September (conservative snow-free indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>There is no formal operating season. Snow, saturated tundra, mosquitoes and river levels vary sharply; obtain current local conditions.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sisimiut centre</td><td>Bike</td><td>~15 min to dirt tracks</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://visitgreenland.com/activities/biking/">Visit Greenland's official biking guide</a> and its <a href="https://visitgreenland.com/destinations/sisimiut/">Sisimiut destination and trail overview</a>. Ask a local operator which tracks are currently appropriate to ride.</i>]]></description>
