  <Placemark>
    <name>Government Peak Recreation Area (Alaska) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Purpose-built Mat-Su singletrack beneath the Talkeetna Mountains</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Two dedicated singletrack trails leave the stadium area and total about 4.2 miles, climbing through forest before rolling downhill. The wider recreation area adds scenic multi-use terrain and views toward the Chugach Range. This is a compact pedal-access trail network, not the proposed downhill ski development on the other side of Government Peak.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift or shuttle. Pedal the two-way singletrack from the chalet and yield to uphill riders and pedestrians. Borough parking is 5 USD per day or 40 USD for an annual pass according to the published trail brochure.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 June; closed from 1 October (typical dry-trail indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>Opening is condition-dependent. Do not ride saturated trails, and expect lingering snow or freeze-thaw outside midsummer.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Palmer</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Anchorage</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://matsu.gov/trails/gpra">Matanuska-Susitna Borough trail description and status</a>. Check the live Borough status before riding.</i>]]></description>
