  <Placemark>
    <name>Eaglecrest Flow Trail (Alaska) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Unsupervised downhill flow trail on Douglas Island</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Eaglecrest maintains a dedicated, signed downhill-only mountain-bike flow trail in its lush coastal mountain setting. The present summer offer is a pedal-access trail rather than the larger lift-served bike park shown in long-term development plans. Inspect features on the first lap and expect wet roots, soft ground and active mountain maintenance nearby.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No summer lift or supervised bike operation is documented. Pedal the service-road access from the ski-area base; riding is at your own risk and hikers are prohibited on the bike trail.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 1 October (typical snow-free indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>There is no formal bike-park calendar. Obey posted closures and check the current mountain report because snow, saturated ground and maintenance can block access.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Downtown Juneau</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://skieaglecrest.com/info/">official Eaglecrest mountain-bike flow-trail rules</a> and <a href="https://skieaglecrest.com/conditions/">official mountain conditions</a>. The winter chairs should not be assumed to carry bikes.</i>]]></description>
