  <Placemark>
    <name>Kereita Forest MTB Park (Kenya) [no lift, shuttle days]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kenya's established downhill and enduro forest venue</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Maintained mountain-bike trails wind through high-elevation Kereita Forest on the Aberdare slopes. The network includes purpose-built descents, technical forest riding and a skills area, with loops ranging from approachable trail riding to intermediate and expert gravity terrain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No mechanical lift. Pedal the loops or confirm locally advertised Saturday shuttle laps. Published 2026 indications are around 300 KES forest entry and 500 KES for the trails; bike hire and coaching are available through the operator.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 January with no formal seasonal closure.<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated venue hours. Heavy rain makes roots and soil extremely slippery; confirm opening, shuttle operation and fees before travelling.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Nairobi</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://theforest.co.ke/mountain-biking/">The Forest's official mountain-biking page</a> and <a href="https://cycleafricabikes.com/cycling-routes-nairobi/">Cycle Africa's 2026 Kereita trail and shuttle guide</a>. Confirm forest conditions and access locally.</i>]]></description>
