  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Wakan Titan of the Hill (Oman) [historic race, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Steep Hajar Mountain enduro race terrain</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The cliffside village of Wakan hosted the first Red Bull Titan of the Hill downhill and enduro competition in 2017. Rocky mountain paths, tight village terrain and severe exposure made it a striking race venue, but there is no documented permanent signed course or routine bike operation today.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift or regular shuttle. The village approach requires a capable vehicle and any riding requires current local permission and a guide who can avoid pedestrian steps, orchards and private areas.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Do not ride the village's walking stairway or assume an old event course remains legal. Exposure, loose rock, extreme heat and flash floods are serious hazards.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 October; closed from 1 May (cooler-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: guided daylight access only<br/><small>No formal operating season or maintained race line is documented.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Muscat</td><td>4x4 / local guide</td><td>~2h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the <a href="https://www.redbull.com/mea-en/events/red-bull-titan-of-the-hill">Red Bull event record</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wakan,_Oman">Wakan access and race-venue reference</a>. Verify all present-day access locally.</i>]]></description>
