  <Placemark>
    <name>Altai Tavan Bogd Downhill Expedition (Mongolia) [4x4 supported, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Choose-your-line freeride in Mongolia's Altai</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A fully supported expedition format uses the immense Tavan Bogd landscape for natural downhill runs rather than fixed trails. Riders choose descents across open alpine slopes, rock and remote valleys, linking camps in terrain where there is effectively no MTB infrastructure.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Russian 4x4 vans with bike racks provide expedition support. A published 2026 package ranges from 2880 USD per person for five or six riders to 4450 USD for two, including domestic flights, guides, vehicles, camping and park fees.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; This is remote expedition freeride with river crossings, severe weather and very limited rescue. Do not attempt it without permits, guides, communications and a complete support team.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 16 September (published 2026 expedition window).<br/>Daily opening hours: expedition schedule<br/><small>Snow, flooding and local park restrictions can alter routes at short notice.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Ulaanbaatar</td><td>Flight to Ölgii + 4x4</td><td>Multi-day approach</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.mongoliabiking.com/tour/downhill-biking-trip-in-altai-mountains">published 2026 supported Altai downhill expedition</a>. Confirm permits, insurance, equipment and exact itinerary with the operator.</i>]]></description>
