  <Placemark>
    <name>Bogd Khan Mountain Trails (Mongolia) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Natural descents immediately above Ulaanbaatar</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Local riders use the forested northern valleys and open southern slopes of the Bogd Khan reserve for natural downhill and trail riding. Routes toward Tsetsee Gun involve steep climbing, rock gardens and shared hiking paths; there is no official bike park, trail grading or unified MTB map.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift or established shuttle. Pedal from the city edge or arrange a local rider or guide who knows current reserve rules and suitable descents.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; This is a protected nature reserve. Use only routes currently open to bicycles, avoid fragile or muddy ground and yield to every walker. Seasonal closures occur.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 June; closed from 1 October (snow-free indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>No formal operating season. Check reserve closures, fire restrictions and trail conditions locally.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Central Ulaanbaatar</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://visitulaanbaatar.net/storage/files/Guide%20book%2020211026.pdf">Ulaanbaatar tourism's cycling and outdoor guide</a> and the <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/mongolia/comments/1mbcmev/">local rider summary of Bogd and Terelj downhill access</a>. Verify permitted routes with a local cycling group.</i>]]></description>
