  <Placemark>
    <name>Kalaw to Inle Highlands (Myanmar) [travel warning, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Shan Plateau singletrack and plantation descents</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Guided cycling itineraries from Kalaw cross rolling Shan highlands, tea plantations, farms and village paths before descending toward Inle Lake. Sections use dirt roads and genuine singletrack, but this is shared rural adventure riding rather than a maintained gravity park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Local operators historically offered mountain-bike hire, guides and vehicle support. Confirm that a reputable operator is currently functioning and that the entire itinerary is lawful and safe before booking.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; As of July 2026, official advice warns against all but essential travel to southern and eastern Shan State. Conflict is volatile, restrictions can change without notice and rural landmine risk exists. Do not plan this ride while advice remains in force.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 November; closed from 1 May (dry-season indication only).<br/>Daily opening hours: guided daylight access only<br/><small>This seasonal metadata describes climate, not a declaration that travel is currently safe or open.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Heho</td><td>Pre-arranged operator vehicle</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: a <a href="https://www.go-myanmar.com/node/1271">documented Kalaw and Inle mountain-bike itinerary</a> and the <a href="https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/myanmar">current official Myanmar travel warning</a>. Reassess security and operator status before any travel.</i>]]></description>
