  <Placemark>
    <name>Banco Forest MTB Loop (Côte d'Ivoire) [no lift, verify park access]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Rainforest trail riding inside Abidjan</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Community-recorded MTB loops use the roads and paths around Banco National Park's lake and Maison de la Nature, creating about 20 km of rolling forest riding with roughly 210 m of climbing. It is cross-country leaning rather than a gravity park, but includes short natural descents in dense tropical forest.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal the loop and confirm at the park entrance which paths currently allow bicycles; visitor rules and protected zones take priority over old GPS recordings.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Stay only on authorized routes, yield to walkers and never enter closed forest. Do not ride after heavy rain.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 November; closed from 1 May (drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-16:00<br/><small>Estimated park-daylight window. Verify current admission and bicycle rules.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Central Abidjan</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.komoot.com/guide/9056/mtb-trails-in-cote-d-ivoire/">documented Banco forest MTB loop and statistics</a>. Confirm present park access with staff before riding.</i>]]></description>
