  <Placemark>
    <name>Freetown Peninsula Mountains (Sierra Leone) [scouting only, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Steep rainforest relief above the Atlantic</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Western Area Peninsula Forest Reserve rises sharply behind Freetown, with rough mountain roads and hiking routes toward Picket Hill, Mount Gabon and coastal villages. The terrain is potentially compelling for natural enduro, but no signed MTB network, maintained descent or dependable bicycle guide is documented.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift or shuttle. Do not use this approximate pin as a trailhead; first arrange a local outdoor guide, land permission and a route confirmed appropriate for bicycles.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Protected rainforest, extreme wet-season mud, heat and limited rescue make unsupported exploration inappropriate. Give way to every walker and community user.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 November; closed from 1 May (drier-season indication only).<br/>Daily opening hours: guided daylight access only<br/><small>No formal MTB operating season exists.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Freetown</td><td>Local guide / vehicle</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.visitsierraleone.org/western-area-peninsula-forest-reserve-a-gem-for-ecotourists-and-explorers/">peninsula mountain and trail overview</a> and <a href="https://tourismsierraleone.com/stories/cycling-in-sierra-leone/">Sierra Leone Tourism's cycling guidance</a>. This is a candidate natural area, not an endorsed route.</i>]]></description>
