  <Placemark>
    <name>Chinguetti / Adrar Desert MTB (Mauritania) [expedition, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Rocky plateau and dune expedition riding</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Adrar around Chinguetti combines sandstone plateaus, abrupt escarpments, rocky pistes and the Ouarane dunes. Community cycling records include long MTB-capable routes around Chinguetti, but this is remote desert expedition terrain rather than signed singletrack or a gravity park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. A 4x4 support vehicle, local desert guide, satellite communication, water and a route chosen around current security restrictions are essential.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Heat, navigation, mine-risk border areas and rapidly changing military zones can be fatal. Official advice restricts parts of Adrar and eastern Mauritania. Never improvise a route or travel without current local authority advice.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 November; closed from 1 April (cooler-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: expedition schedule<br/><small>Ride only in cool daylight windows; sandstorms and security changes can cancel travel.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Atar</td><td>4x4 support</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.bikemap.net/en/l/2381972/">documented Adrar cycling routes</a>, <a href="https://www.chingitours.com/fr/spot/adrar-fr/">Adrar terrain and local expedition season</a> and <a href="https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mauritania/regional-risks">current regional travel restrictions</a>.</i>]]></description>
