  <Placemark>
    <name>Bagofit MTB Circuit (Cameroon) [race venue, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Cameroon's established forest MTB race circuit</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Bagofit Sun City hosts the Chantal Biya mountain-bike race on a rugged 15 km circuit. About 5 km runs through forest, with laterite, tree trunks, water holes and mud forming the principal obstacles. This is an event and cross-country-oriented course with short natural descents, not a permanent lift-served bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift or documented public shuttle. Contact Bagofit Sun City or the race organizer before travelling: access to the complete competition circuit outside an event has not been confirmed.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Do not assume the race course is marked, maintained or open year-round. Tropical rain can make its water and mud obstacles unsafe.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 December; closed from 1 May (drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: contact the venue<br/><small>The annual race can occur outside this weather window; published 2026 event dates are 7-8 August.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bertoua</td><td>Car to Bagofit Sun City</td><td>~2h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.cameroon-tribune.cm/article.html/61634/fr.html/cyclisme-bagofit-vitesse">Cameroon Tribune's 15 km course description</a> and <a href="https://crtv.cm/news/news/east-region-3rd-chantal-biya-international-mountain-bike-race-launched">CRTV's current international race announcement</a>. Confirm public riding access directly with the venue.</i>]]></description>
