  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Djibloho / Oyala MTB Loop (Equatorial Guinea) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Documented mainland MTB loop around Ciudad de la Paz</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Djibloho community route is a 9.2 km mountain-bike loop with about 104 m of climbing around the planned city formerly known as Oyala. It offers rolling tropical dirt-road and track exploration, not a signed bike park or sustained downhill venue. Only a handful of public MTB recordings exist in the country, so current local knowledge is essential.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift, shuttle or trail fee is documented. Ride under your own power and confirm that each road or track remains publicly accessible.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Treat the GPS recording as a route reference, not proof of access or maintenance. Carry water and offline navigation, avoid construction and government zones, and obtain permission before entering private land.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 December; closed from 1 March (drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>No formal MTB operating calendar exists.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Mongomeyén Airport</td><td>Car with local contact</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the <a href="https://es.wikiloc.com/rutas-mountain-bike/djibloho-14375427">recorded 9.2 km Djibloho MTB loop</a> and the <a href="https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/65b78d77a0ae1b0012526157/Equatorial_Guinea_Toponymic_Factfile.pdf">official toponymic reference linking Oyala, Djibloho and Ciudad de la Paz</a>. Verify access locally.</i>]]></description>
