  <Placemark>
    <name>Mabira Forest MTB Trail (Uganda) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Dedicated rainforest loop between Kampala and Jinja</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Mabira Central Forest Reserve has an established 25 km mountain-bike loop linking rainforest trails with surrounding tea and sugar plantations. It is rolling adventure and cross-country terrain with roots, clay and short natural descents rather than a gravity park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift or regular shuttle. Ride from the Najjembe visitor centre; local guided tours can include a mountain bike, helmet, food and water. Older published entry prices are not reliable enough to quote, so confirm fees and bike availability before arrival.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; This is a protected forest with shared paths. Register at the visitor centre, remain on the authorized bicycle route, yield to walkers and avoid wet trails.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 June; closed from 1 October (one of Uganda's drier riding windows).<br/>Daily opening hours: guided daylight access only<br/><small>The reserve operates year-round, but rain can make clay, roots and stream crossings unsuitable.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Jinja</td><td>Car / taxi to Najjembe</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Kampala</td><td>Car / taxi</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the <a href="https://ugandatourismcenter.com/place/mabira-forest">documented 25 km forest MTB loop and access guide</a> and <a href="https://www.jinjabiketoursandsafaris.org/">local guided Mabira bike tours</a>. Confirm current reserve rules locally.</i>]]></description>
