  <Placemark>
    <name>Mukura Forest Bike Trail (Rwanda) [guide required, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Highland forest riding on Rwanda's Congo-Nile divide</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Rwanda's tourism planning identifies a dedicated Mukura Bike Trail in the forest and highlands east of Lake Kivu. Expect steep rural tracks, roots and wet montane terrain rather than a maintained gravity network; detailed public grading and a current standalone trail map are limited.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift or permanent shuttle. Arrange a trained cycling guide and verify the approved route, park entry and bicycle permission before travelling.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Mukura is protected forest habitat. Do not improvise on walking or wildlife trails, ride alone, or enter without current authorization.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 June; closed from 1 October (principal dry-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: guided daylight access only<br/><small>No independently verified operating calendar is published.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Rubavu</td><td>Guide vehicle</td><td>~2h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the <a href="https://rema.gov.rw/rema_doc/LAFREC/GMNP%20TOURISM%20DEVELOPMENT%20MASTER%20PLAN%20Nov%202018.pdf">official Gishwati-Mukura tourism plan listing the Mukura Bike Trail</a> and the <a href="https://rdb.rw/rdb-tourism-launches-mountain-biking/">Rwanda Development Board cycling program</a>. Confirm access with park authorities.</i>]]></description>
