  <Placemark>
    <name>Station VTT du Volcan (Réunion) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>126 km of graded volcanic mountain-bike routes</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The official Volcan MTB station has 12 rehabilitated circuits across 126 km on the Piton de la Fournaise massif; all 12 official ONF traces are drawn on this map. Green, blue, red and black routes support loop, descent and enduro riding through pasture, forest and stark volcanic landscapes. The marker is at Piton Textor, the principal hub and official start for six circuits.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No bike lift or permanent uplift is documented. Pedal the signed loops or arrange a local guide and vehicle for a route designed as a descent. Public trail access is generally free.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Volcanic activity, fire risk, fog and ONF forestry orders can close roads or trails without warning. Use the official carto-guide and obey every closure.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 May; closed from 1 December (cooler and generally drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>The network is normally year-round when authorized, but exposed high routes are weather dependent.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Saint-Pierre</td><td>Car to Piton Textor</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: the <a href="https://www.onf.fr/vivre-la-foret/%2B/16b8%3A%3Apistes-vtt-et-vttae-au-volcan-la-reunion.html?lang=fr">official ONF Volcan circuit guide, trailheads and GPX downloads</a>. Check volcanic and forestry access before departure.</i>]]></description>
