  <Placemark>
    <name>Valle Nevado Bike Park (Chile) [chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Valle Nevado 3000 m - lift-served gravity in the Andes above Santiago</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>South America's highest lift-served bike park, with downhill and enduro trails on the slopes above Santiago at 3000+ m altitude. The thin air, rocky terrain and views of the Aconcagua range make this a unique high-alpine destination. Shared access with neighbouring El Colorado and Farellones.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Andersen gondola and chairlifts carry bikes during the December-March summer season. Confirm the current bike pass and lift schedule with Valle Nevado before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from December; closed from March (southern hemisphere summer).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Santiago</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.vallenevado.com/en/summer/bike-park/">Valle Nevado</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
