  <Placemark>
    <name>Bike Park Kranjska Gora (Julian Alps, SI) [day rate unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Vitranc 2 top station 1560 m - the upper drop-in</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Slovenia's first official bike park, open since 2004, and still the country's main gravity venue - it hosted a round of the iXS European Downhill Cup in 2025. Close to 20 km of trails over four zones (Kekec, Vitranc 1, Brsnina and Vitranc 2), from easy flow through jump lines to steep technical downhill. The Vitranc 2 chair, opened for summer more recently, roughly doubles the vertical to around 740 m off the top.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Vitranc 1 and Vitranc 2 both carry bikes. Last ride up from Vitranc 1 is 16:45; Vitranc 2 runs 09:30-16:00. The operator had not published a 2026 price list at the time of writing, so no day rate is recorded here - check ski-kranjska-gora.com before you go. Downhill and enduro rentals through MTB Republic at the base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 20 May; closed from 30 September (typical window; check the operator and conditions). Daily operation 25 June to 31 August 2026.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Ljubljana</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Villach</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://ski-kranjska-gora.com/en/summer/bike-park">SKI Kranjska Gora</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
