  <Placemark>
    <name>Mayrhofen - Penken (Zillertal, AT) [72.50 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Penken 1790 m - top of the Penkenbahn</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Zillertal's gravity centre, and home of the Hoellenritt - a purpose-built singletrail that drops the full mountain back to Mayrhofen and is one of the longest of its kind in the Alps. Himmelfahrt is the second signature line. Above them the Penken plateau feeds panorama routes and all-mountain trails, and the Ahorn on the far side of the valley adds more. Not a lines-and-berms bike park so much as a very large lift-served trail mountain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Penkenbahn from Mayrhofen carries bikes, backed up by the Horbergbahn and the Finkenberger Almbahn. The Action Day Ticket for bikers is 72.50 EUR (63 EUR with the Zillertal guest card, 31.50 EUR child); a plain up-and-down is 40 EUR and a single ride 28 EUR.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 23 May; closed from 4 October (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Innsbruck</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Munich</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.mayrhofen.at/en/stories/mountopolis-mountainbiking">Mayrhofner Bergbahnen</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
