  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Belleville - Les Menuires and Val Thorens (Savoie, FR) [26.70 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Pointe de la Masse 2770 m - top of the La Masse gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Belleville valley - Les Menuires, Saint-Martin and Val Thorens - runs over 100 km of marked trail between 1400 and 2800 m, the highest lift-served riding in the Trois Vallees. Easy Rider and Kiss Cool are the approachable descents; High Line and B'Hell'Ville Line are the serious ones, and a large enduro network links the three villages. From La Masse the descent is unbroken from 2770 m to 1400 m, all of it above or at the treeline.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Pointe de la Masse gondola from Les Menuires is the key lift; Bruyeres and the Val Thorens lifts extend the terrain. A VTT day pass for the Trois Vallees bike area is 26.70 EUR, and winter season-pass holders get summer lift access included.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 5 July; closed from 31 August (published 2026 dates - a short high-summer season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:15-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Geneva</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr><tr><td>Moutiers</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://lesmenuires.com/en/bike-park">Les Menuires</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
