  <Placemark>
    <name>Antur Stiniog (Eryri / Snowdonia, Wales) [44 GBP]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Uplift drop-off 470 m - above Blaenau Ffestiniog</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Fourteen downhill tracks cut into old slate workings above Blaenau Ffestiniog, green through to black, and there is no pedalling to them - the uplift is the only way up. Around 200 m of vertical per run, which sounds modest until you find the tracks are steep, rocky and relentless. Big tabletops and doubles on the graded jump lines, raw slate and roots on the black tracks. Five minutes up, ten to twenty down, and up to twenty runs in a day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Van uplift only, roughly 40 to 44 GBP for the day; the trails cannot be ridden without it. Full facilities at the visitor centre: cafe, bike wash, showers and parking. Book ahead, it sells out.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open all year (uplift days are typically Thursday to Sunday; check the calendar before travelling).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Manchester</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr><tr><td>Llandudno</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.anturstiniog.com/">Antur Stiniog</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
