  <Placemark>
    <name>Revolution Bike Park (Llangynog, Wales) [50 GBP]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Llangynog 280 m - Revolution Bike Park, van uplift to the top</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 20 km of trail on a steep Berwyn hillside, and the reason people drive here is the jump lines: some of the biggest built anywhere in the UK. Alongside them sit raw, rooty natural tracks that stay genuinely hard in the wet, which in mid Wales is most of the time. This is not a beginner venue - full-face helmets and knee pads are compulsory for everyone.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Van uplift, 50 GBP for the day, or 15 GBP for a push-up pass; extra single lifts are 5 GBP each subject to space, with day-ticket holders given priority. Booking in advance on the website is required.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open all year, Friday to Sunday (check the website - conditions close the hill).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Manchester</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr><tr><td>Shrewsbury</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h10</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.revolutionbike-park.co.uk/">Revolution Bike Park</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-3.409510,52.815600,0</coordinates></Point>
