  <Placemark>
    <name>Bike Park Ireland (Co. Tipperary, IE) [uplift rate unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Ballingarry 120 m - Bike Park Ireland, truck uplift to the top</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Ireland's only full gravity bike park with a proper uplift service. Six downhill trails from green to black plus a pro line, eight uplifted tracks in all, a large pump track and an cross-country loop, cut into wooded hillside in north Tipperary. The vertical is small but the tracks are well built and there is enough black-grade tech to keep experienced riders honest.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Three ex-army trucks, each with 30 seats and a bike trailer, run to the top every 15 minutes; a ticket covers park entry plus unlimited uplifts, in half-day or full-day form. We could not reach the operator's current price list, so no rate is recorded here - check bike-parkireland.ie.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open all year, every weekend (office Tuesday to Sunday; weekday riding by arrangement).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Dublin</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr><tr><td>Limerick</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.bike-parkireland.ie/">Bike Park Ireland</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
