  <Placemark>
    <name>Nitehawk Bike Park (Alberta, CA) [28 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Nitehawk 673 m - top of the Bauer Triple Chair</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A gravity park just south of Grande Prairie with green, blue and black lines built around berms, log rides, doubles, skinnies, drops and tabletops. Dirty Deeds (blue, downhill only) is a signature run, with a technical black connector through to O'Brien.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Bauer Triple Chair uplift. Adult full day 28 CAD (half day 25 CAD), children 12 and under full day 22 CAD (half day 20 CAD).<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 20 May; closed from 30 August (typical window; check the operator before travel).<br/>Daily opening hours: Wed 17:30-21:00, Sat 12:00-17:00<br/><small>Limited weekly schedule; check the operator calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Grande Prairie</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://gonitehawk.com/">Nitehawk Year-Round Adventure Park</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
