  <Placemark>
    <name>Bike Glendhu (Wanaka, NZ) [38 NZD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Glendhu Bay 310 m - Bike Glendhu base, shuttles to the summit</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Close to 40 km of purpose-built trail on a working high-country sheep station above Lake Wanaka, opened in 2020 and already one of the best trail networks in New Zealand. Long, cruisey scenic climbs and descents for beginners at the bottom, hard singletrack and jump lines higher up, and the whole thing looks out over the lake and the Southern Alps. Dry schist soil that rides year-round.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A day trail pass is 38 NZD for adults, 32 NZD concession; season and multi-day passes are better value if you stay. You can pedal everything, or take a van shuttle to the lower mountain or a Can-Am buggy boost to the summit - shuttles need booking 48 hours ahead and run only when conditions allow.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open all year (trail conditions and shuttles vary with the weather).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Wanaka</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Queenstown</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://bikeglendhu.co.nz/passes/">Bike Glendhu</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>169.003760,-44.673200,0</coordinates></Point>
