  <Placemark>
    <name>Sandy Ridge Trail System (Oregon) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sandy Ridge 320 m - main trailhead of the Sandy Ridge Trail System</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>BLM describes about 17 miles of directional, downhill-only singletrack designed for mountain bikers in the Cascade foothills west of Mount Hood. The range runs from machine-built beginner flow trails with rollers and table tops to double-black expert lines with exposure, rock gardens, steep grades and jump lines. Mapped named descents include Hide and Seek, Follow The Leader, Quid Pro Flow, Communication Breakdown, Two Turntables and a Microwave, Flow Motion, Rock Drop, Johnny Royale, TNT, Little Monkey and Laura's Loop.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. The system is pedal-accessed: ride up the gated Homestead Road (paved, roughly 3-4 miles) to the upper trailhead. A parking pass is required at the main lot: $5/day for a passenger car, $10 for a van, $20 for a bus, or $30/year Northwest Oregon District pass. Buy at the kiosk or via Recreation.gov.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round, dawn to dusk. The access road and upper trails can be snow-covered in mid-winter; the trails generally hold up well in wet conditions.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Portland</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Sandy</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Portland / Sandy</td><td>SAM MHX bus + bike</td><td>~1 h 30 + short ride</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.blm.gov/programs/recreation/mountainbike/sandyridge">BLM Sandy Ridge</a>, <a href="https://www.mtbproject.com/trail/3482113/sandy-ridge-full-tour">MTB Project - Sandy Ridge Full Tour</a>, <a href="https://nw-trail.org/trails/sandy-ridge/">Northwest Trail Alliance</a>, <a href="https://www.ci.sandy.or.us/community/page/sandy-ridge-trail-system">City of Sandy</a>.</i>]]></description>
