  <Placemark>
    <name>Post Canyon - Hood River (Oregon) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Pedal-accessed freeride and enduro trail network above Hood River at ~321 m</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>About 25 mi / 40 km of singletrack ranging from mellow flow to expert wooden features. Notable trails include Seven Streams, Family Man skills park, Grand Prix, Bad Motor Scooter, Charley's Loop, Mitchell Ridge, Mobius, 140 Trail, Kleeway, Float On, Spaghetti Factory, Thee Way, Cardiac Bypass and Donkey Boy. Rides best as a clockwise loop; the lower canyon is beginner-friendly while the upper forest holds the freeride lines.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal up or arrange a local shuttle. A Hood River County Forest parking permit is required at Seven Streams, Post Flats, Family Man, Binns Hill, Kingsley and Pinemont staging areas: $45 annual / $10 daily (effective July 2026), available online and from local vendors.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 January; closed from 31 December (ridable year-round, best spring-fall). Summers are dry; winters are wet and muddy. Fire-season restrictions can close motorized access and sometimes trails; check current regulations before visiting.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Hood River</td><td>Car / bike</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Portland</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.singletracks.com/bike-trails/post-canyon/">Singletracks Post Canyon</a>, <a href="https://www.hoodrivercounty.gov/forestry">Hood River County Forestry</a>, <a href="https://www.hoodrivercounty.gov/parking-permit-details">HRC parking permit details</a>, <a href="https://visithoodriver.com/">Visit Hood River</a>.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-121.6006680,45.6946824,0</coordinates></Point>
