  <Placemark>
    <name>Black Rock Mountain Bike Area (Oregon) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Black Rock MTB parking, ~215 m</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Purpose-built freeride and DH lines on Mt. Brown in the Coast Range. Banzai Downhill is a rollable green/blue flow line with tabletops and ride-arounds; Sickter Gnar is a black mix of drops, jumps, rocks and tech. The signature expert-only trails are Granny's Kitchen, Sunday Stroll, Brake Check, The Runaround and Player Slayer, with wooden features, mandatory gaps and big-freeride moves. Basic Training is an all-levels skills area for drops and jumps.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - all climbing is under your own power. Parking at the trailhead is free. BRMBA is a volunteer-run 501(c)(3) nonprofit; donations support trail building and maintenance.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round. Coast Range winters are wet and trails can become muddy; actual rideability depends on weather and conditions.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Portland</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h55</td></tr><tr><td>Salem</td><td>Car</td><td>~55 min</td></tr><tr><td>McMinnville</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h05</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.brmba.org/trails/">BRMBA trails</a>, <a href="https://www.brmba.org/about-us/">BRMBA about us</a>, <a href="https://www.brmba.org/rider-conduct/">BRMBA rider conduct</a>, <a href="https://www.oregon.gov/odf/recreation/Pages/default.aspx">ODF recreation</a>. Verify conditions, rules and access before riding.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
