  <Placemark>
    <name>Skeggs Point / El Corte de Madera Creek Preserve [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Skeggs Point 709 m - trailhead</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>El Corte de Madera Creek Preserve, locally called Skeggs Point, is a 2,908-acre redwood-forest network with 34+ miles of multi-use trail (about 20 miles singletrack and 14 miles fire road). Bike-legal highlights include Sierra Morena, Oljon, Resolution, North Leaf, Manzanita, Giant Salamander, Blue Blossom, Fir, Methuselah and Timberview. Difficulty ranges from mellow intermediate singletrack to steep, technical, rocky sections that many riders hike-a-bike; Fir Trail and some others are really only fun downhill. Helmets are required, the trail speed limit is 15 mph, and e-bikes are not allowed. Check current trail status before riding, as some trails close seasonally for wet weather or salamander protection.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift - every climb is earned. Park free at the Skeggs Point vista-point lot (26 spaces, across Skyline Blvd from the trailhead) or at the El Corte de Madera Parking Area (65 spaces, about 0.4 mi south). Restrooms are available at the main El Corte de Madera lot. Bring a map or GPS; the dense network is easy to get lost in.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open a half-hour before sunrise until a half-hour after sunset, year-round. Expect heavy coastal fog and winter wet-weather closures, especially on Giant Salamander Trail. Verify current conditions on the Midpen website before heading out.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>San Francisco</td><td>Car</td><td>~55 min</td></tr><tr><td>Redwood City</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>San Jose</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.openspace.org/preserves/el-corte-de-madera-creek">Midpeninsula Regional Open Space District</a>, <a href="https://www.mtbproject.com/trail/7040247/skeggs-n-eggs">MTB Project</a>, <a href="https://sfbayareamountainbiking.com/regional-finder/penninsula-south/el-corte-de-madera-creek-midpeninsula-regional-open-space-skeggs-point/">SF Bay Area Mountain Biking</a>, <a href="https://bayarearides.com/rides/skeggs1/">Bay Area Mountain Bike Rides</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
