  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Murciélagos Bike Park (Puebla) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bottom shuttle base / Hostelería El Trébol 1,690 m</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Steep mountainside bike park in Ajalpan, Puebla, featuring 10 sustainable trails built for Enduro and Downhill mountain biking. The network is fully optimised to support e-bikes. Standout descents include Coyote, a massive 5-mile long downhill singletrack featuring switchbacks, tight speed segments and 3,416 feet of raw descent, plus Aguacate, a fast, highly technical rock-strewn trail.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Vehicular shuttle trucks and e-bike friendly. Riders check in at Hostelería El Trébol hostel, where maintenance fees are paid and vehicle shuttles, local guides or lodging can be arranged. Price not verified here; check the operator.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 November (estimated typical season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-18:00<br/>
    <small>Estimated hours; confirm current shuttle schedules and hostel services with the operator.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Puebla</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mexico City</td><td>Car</td><td>~3 h 30</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: local trail network information and hostel operator reports. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-97.1643,18.4116,0</coordinates></Point>
