  <Placemark>
    <name>Punta Venado Bike Park (Playa del Carmen) [510 MXN]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Main basecamp and shop - coastal highway Km 278</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Premier specialised mountain bike park in the Yucatan Peninsula. Contains 20 singletrack trails weaving through coastal mangroves and thick jungle. Unlike mountainous parks, this is a Cross-Country (XC) network built entirely over rugged, unforgiving fossilised coral reefs, simulating high technical handling without major elevation. Standout lines include Del Jaguar #7 and the Earthquake Trail, both physical, punchy lines packed with jagged limestone rock gardens. Loops uniquely finish directly on a Caribbean beach.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Strictly pedal-powered cross-country over completely flat landscape. Standard international trail access approximately 510 MXN (~$30 USD), with premium full-suspension bike rentals available on-site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; closed Mondays.<br/>Daily opening hours: 07:00-15:00 (Tuesday to Sunday)<br/>
    <small>Published operating hours; closed on Mondays. Confirm current schedules and rental availability.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Playa del Carmen</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Cancún</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: park operator official information and regional trail network documentation. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
