  <Placemark>
    <name>Martigny / Vallee du Trient MTB [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Martigny route trailhead - pedal-powered loops</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Two substantial official MTB loops start in Martigny. Le Planard is a 27 km intermediate circuit with about 1,065 m of climbing over Mont Chemin and the Col des Planches. The 40.5 km Tour de la Vallee du Trient is a difficult all-day route with about 1,705 m of climbing through Vernayaz, Les Marecottes, Le Tretien, Finhaut and the Col de la Forclaz. These are mixed-surface mountain tours rather than purpose-built downhill runs; expect shared paths and roads.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up</b><br/>There is no verified bike-park uplift for these routes. Both are designed as pedal-powered loops from Martigny.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Le Planard is generally suitable from spring through autumn. The higher Trient loop is published for early July to mid-October; check snow and trail conditions.<br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.martigny.com/fr/activity/le-planard-vtt-44920/">Le Planard</a> and <a href="https://www.martigny.com/fr/activity/tour-de-la-vallee-du-trient-vtt-44848/">Tour de la Vallee du Trient</a>, Martigny Tourism.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-red</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>7.073844,46.101349,0</coordinates></Point>
